You should bring back prototype.js since it's essential for the
webapp. Prototype is a JavaScript library, check out the homepage:
http://www.prototypejs.org/

However, Prototype is requred because of Ajax.Updater object defined
in Prototype library - it's responsible for asynchronous calls (http://
www.w3schools.com/ajax/default.asp <http://www.w3schools.com/ajax/default.asp>). However, you don't need Prototype
for AJAX calls, just follow w3schools tutorials on JavaScript and
AJAX, and try to write your own code using plain JavaScript. It's a
good practice.

